# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""Lecture 43 objective pool A -- Pulmonary Nodules and Neoplasms (Gray): epidemiology, risk factors and spread
(slides 3-10); incidental nodules and presenting symptoms (slides 11-13); diagnostic workup and biopsy
(slides 14-15).

KEYS ARE WRITTEN SHORT ON PURPOSE -- detail lives in the explanation.
EXPLANATIONS follow tools/question_writing/EXPLAIN_DEEP.md (Jaxon, 2026-10-29): the key names the decisive
clue and the fact; each wrong choice says why it fails here, the replacing fact, and a tell.

Set 1 is recall against the syllabus objectives, so no stem carries a patient age. Scope caps and the slide
conflicts that are never keyed live in cms_e7l43_scope.py. Every key is a slide fact; Gray corrected no slide
out loud, so nothing here rests on a spoken correction. Slide 5 (node map) and slide 7 (histology) are excluded
and never cited. The women's mortality rank (slide 3), the adenocarcinoma percentages (slides 4 and 31) and the
probability-of-malignancy percentages (slide 11) are never asked; the solid-nodule algorithm is asked by its
classes in words.
"""
import os, sys
sys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))
from _cmse3_q import Q
from cms_e7l43_scope import *


def S(topic, io, q, opts, cite, slot):
    d = Q(topic, io, q, opts, cite); d["slot"] = slot; return d


def ORD(d, asc):
    d["ordered"] = True; d["asc"] = asc; return d


